# =============================================================================
# HOW TO USE THIS FILE
# =============================================================================
# 1. Copy this file to ".env.local" in the same folder (project root).
#    PowerShell:  Copy-Item .env.example .env.local
# 2. Replace every placeholder below with your real values.
# 3. NEVER commit .env.local to git (it is already in .gitignore).
# 4. After changing env vars, restart "npm run dev" (Next.js reads them at startup).
#
# =============================================================================
# A) SUPABASE — create project & keys
# =============================================================================
# 1. Go to https://supabase.com → New project → wait until the DB is ready.
# 2. Dashboard → Project Settings (gear) → API:
#    - "Project URL"  → NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL (must start with https://)
#    - "anon public"  → NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY (safe in browser; still protect your repo)
#    - "service_role" → SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY (SECRET: server/CI only, never in client code)
# 3. Apply the database schema:
#    - If you use Supabase CLI:  supabase link  then  npm run db:migrate  (or: supabase db push)
#    - Or: Dashboard → SQL Editor → paste contents of:
#      supabase/migrations/001_initial_schema.sql → Run
#    - If "create extension pg_cron / pg_net" errors: Dashboard → Database → Extensions
#      enable pg_cron and pg_net, then re-run the migration or only the extension lines + rest.
# 4. Realtiashboard → Database → Replication → enable for table "reminders" me (optional, for live list updates):
#    - D(public schema).
#
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key

SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-supabase-service-role-key

# Worker (Bull) can read either NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL or this explicit var:
# SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co

# =============================================================================
# B) PUBLIC APP URL — used by Twilio & edge functions for callbacks
# =============================================================================
# Must be the base URL where THIS Next.js app is reachable (no trailing slash).
# Examples:
#   Local tunnel for Twilio testing: https://xxxx.ngrok.io
#   Production: https://reminders.yourdomain.com
# Twilio will POST call status to:  WEBHOOK_URL + "/api/twilio-status"
# Edge function process-reminder uses WEBHOOK_URL (set as Supabase secret too — see manual steps).
#
WEBHOOK_URL=https://your-app.netlify.app
# =============================================================================
# C) RESEND — transactional email
# =============================================================================
# 1. https://resend.com → sign up → API Keys → create key → RESEND_API_KEY
# 2. Domains → add & verify your domain (DNS records).
# 3. FROM_EMAIL must use a verified domain, e.g.:
#    notifications@mail.yourdomain.com
#    (Format can be:  Name <email@domain.com>  in worker; edge function uses RESEND_FROM secret.)
#
RESEND_API_KEY=re_your_resend_api_key
FROM_EMAIL=notifications@mail.yourdomain.com

# Supabase Edge Function "process-reminder" reads this secret if you set it (recommended):
#   supabase secrets set RESEND_FROM="Reminders <noreply@mail.yourdomain.com>"
# If unset, the function falls back to a placeholder — change that in code or always set the secret.

# =============================================================================
# D) TWILIO — voice (and optional SMS via worker)
# =============================================================================
# 1. https://console.twilio.com → copy Account SID and Auth Token.
# 2. Phone Numbers → Buy or use trial number → TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER in E.164: +15551234567
# 3. Trial: you can only call/SMS verified numbers (Twilio console → Verified Caller IDs).
# 4. For production, upgrade account and comply with Twilio/regulatory requirements for your country.
#
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=your-twilio-account-sid
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=your-twilio-auth-token
TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER=+15551234567

# =============================================================================
# E) REDIS — only if you run the Bull worker (worker/queue.ts)
# =============================================================================
# Not required for: Next.js UI, Supabase, or Edge Functions alone.
# Required for: npm run worker:dev / Docker worker service.
# Local: install Redis or: docker run -d -p 6379:6379 redis:7-alpine
#
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
